, Inc. the following year. Its current name was adopted in 2007 as the company expanded its focus from computers to consumer electronics. Apple is one of the Big Tech companies. The company was founded to market Wozniak's Apple I personal computer. Its successor, the Apple II, became one of the first successful mass-produced microcomputers. Apple introduced the Lisa in 1983 and the Macintosh in 1984 as some of the first computers to use a graphical user interface and a mouse. By 1985, internal conflicts led to Jobs leaving the company to form NeXT and Wozniak withdrawing to other ventures; John Sculley was CEO for over a decade. In the 1990s, Apple lost considerable market share in the PC industry to the lower-priced Wintel duopoly of Intel-powered PC clones running Windows, and was reporting major losses by 1997. Wikipedia About Apple Inc CEO Tim Cook Employees 166K Founded Apr 1, 1976 Headquarters Cupertino, California, United States Sector Computers, Peripherals, and Software Website - Analyst ratings Based on 30 analysts giving stock ratings to AAPL in the past 3 months Buy Buy 18 Hold 11 Sell 1 search_spark Dive deeper on analyst ratings 12-month forecast Based on 30 Wall Street analysts offering 12 month price targets for AAPL in the last 3 months. Highest Current $308.63 $400.00 ( +29.61% ) Average $324.40 ( +5.11% ) Lowest $250.00 ( -19.00% ) search_spark Dive deeper on price targets Analyst Recommendation Action Price target Projected Date David Vogt UBS Hold Maintained $296.00 -4.1% 07/01/2026 Daniel Ives Wedbush Buy Maintained $400.00 +29.6% 06/26/2026 Erik Woodring Morgan Stanley Buy Maintained $360.00 +16.6% 06/25/2026 Samik Chatterjee J.P. Morgan Buy Maintained $325.00 +5.3% 06/25/2026 Amit Daryanani Evercore ISI Buy Maintained $365.00 +18.3% 06/25/2026 Tim Long Barclays Sell Maintained $253.00 -18% 06/25/2026 Wamsi Mohan Bank of America Securities Buy Maintained $380.00 +23.1% 06/22/2026 Rob Chang CFA KGI Securities Hold Downgraded $315.00 +2.1% 06/22